Design a 2x2 integer Hadamard transform circuit that processes four 15-bit input pairs and generates four corresponding output pairs. The module computes various sums and differences of the inputs to achieve the transformation, facilitating operations commonly used in signal processing and data compression applications. The outputs represent transformed values based on the summation and negation of the inputs, structured in a way to enable applications in areas such as image processing or coding theory.
