description:
Design a 4-bit output module that modifies the most significant bit (MSB) of a 4-bit input signal. The module incorporates a D flip-flop which captures the value of the input MSB and provides an inverted output for the MSB in the output. The lower three bits of the output remain unchanged, effectively resulting in the input signal's MSB being inverted while preserving the other bits.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    output [3:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    output [3:0] out
);// Voltage supply signals
    supply1 VPWR;
    supply0 VGND;
    supply1 VPB ;
    supply0 VNB ;

    // Invert MSB
    assign out[2:0] = in[2:0]; 
    assign out[3] = ~in[3];  // Directly invert MSB instead of using unknown module

endmodule

