Design a read-only memory (ROM) module that stores 256 entries of 16-bit wide data accessible via an 8-bit address input. The module initializes the memory with specific data values and outputs the data corresponding to the input address. This ROM is intended for applications where fixed data retrieval is required, such as firmware or constant data storage in digital systems.
